            <ArticleTitle>Chiral quantum spin liquid on the repulsive Haldane-Hubbard model in square lattices.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>465601</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1088/1361-648X/aa8c65</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this paper, we present a study on the repulsive Haldane-Hubbard model with spin-rotation symmetry in square lattices by deriving non-linear σ model for magnetic states. It is found that a chiral spin liquid state as the ground state of the correlated system exists in the [Formula: see text] topological spin-density wave proposed by Wu et al (2016 J. Phys.: Condens. Matter 28 115602), of which the low energy physics can be determined by the Chern-Simons-Hopf gauge field theory.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
